{
  "description": "Every handshake of the app channel (docs/m2-design.md sections 5 and 10) with fixed keys, as exact bytes: Noise_IK_25519_ChaChaPoly_SHA256 for sessions, Noise_XXpsk3_25519_ChaChaPoly_SHA256 for linking and restore. Run both sides from the keys and the prologue (the IK initiator is given the responder's static public key; the XXpsk3 initiator is given psk at the start, the responder by setPsk right after it reads message 1): writing each payload must give exactly `message`, reading `message` must give `payload`, both sides must end with `handshakeHash`, and after the split each `plaintext` must encrypt to exactly `message` and decrypt back, in the order listed (each direction has its own nonce). Payloads are the UTF-8 JSON of packages/protocol/src/app/handshake.ts and envelope.ts. A link or restore vector's psk and its LinkHello `find` are those of an entry of app-link-secrets.json (QR code, link address, restore) or app-typed-code.json (typed code).",
